 r←new IsLaterThan old
⍝ Returns a 1 when `new` is a later version than `old`, otherwise a 0.\\
⍝ Both must be complete package IDs, and both are assumed to name the same package: this answers
⍝ "is it later?" and not "is it the same package?".
⍝ `SortIndexForPackageIDs` settles every case but one: it removes the beta part before it compares,
⍝ so "group-name-1.2.0-beta-2" and "group-name-1.2.0" look identical to it. Semantic Versioning puts
⍝ a beta *before* the release it leads up to, so that one is decided here.
⍝ Note that "later" is not the same as "different": a Registry may well offer a version that is
⍝ older than the one installed, for example when the installed one was withdrawn or never published.
 :If (RemoveBetaPart new)≡RemoveBetaPart old
     r←(HasBetaPart old)>HasBetaPart new
 :Else
     r←2=⊃⌽SortIndexForPackageIDs old new
 :EndIf
⍝Done
